<title>USA: Conoco, Maraven seek low royalty for $2.2b venture.</title>
<headline>Conoco, Maraven seek low royalty for $2.2b venture.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dupont Co energy unit Conoco and state-owned Petroleos de Venezuela subsidiary Maraven are seeking a sharply reduced royalty for the early years of their $2.2 billion Petrozuata upgrading joint venture, a Maraven official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Oil activities in Venezuela are normally subject to a royalty rate of 16-2/3 percent but the two joint venture partners are looking to pay just one percent for the first nine years.</p>
<p>If the Venezualan government concedes a low royalty for the Petrozuata project it is likely to affect other, similar multi-billion-dollar ventures.</p>
</text>
